Step 1: Install Docker

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker.io
sudo systemctl enable --now docker

Verify Docker:

sudo docker --version

Step 2: Create the Flask project

mkdir flask-docker-app
cd flask-docker-app

Step 3: Create the Python Flask application

cat > app.py <<'EOF'
from flask import Flask, jsonify

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route("/")
def home():
    return """
    <html>
        <head>
            <title>Flask Docker App</title>
        </head>
        <body style="font-family: Arial; text-align: center; margin-top: 100px;">
            <h1>Hello from Python Flask!</h1>
            <h2>Running inside Docker on Ubuntu 🚀</h2>
            <p>Your Dockerized Flask application is working.</p>
        </body>
    </html>
    """

@app.route("/health")
def health():
    return jsonify(status="healthy")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run(host="0.0.0.0", port=5000)
EOF

Step 4: Create the requirements file

cat > requirements.txt <<'EOF'
Flask>=3.1,<4.0
gunicorn>=23.0,<24.0
EOF

Step 5: Create the Dockerfile

cat > Dockerfile <<'EOF'
FROM python:3.12-slim

WORKDIR /app

ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
ENV PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1

COPY requirements.txt .

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt

COPY app.py .

EXPOSE 5000

CMD ["gunicorn", "--bind", "0.0.0.0:5000", "--workers", "2", "app:app"]
EOF

Step 6: Create the Docker ignore file

cat > .dockerignore <<'EOF'
__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
venv
.git
.env
EOF

Step 7: Build the Docker image

sudo docker build -t flask-docker-app .

Step 8: Run the Docker container

sudo docker run -d \
  --name flask-container \
  -p 5000:5000 \
  --restart unless-stopped \
  flask-docker-app

Step 9: Verify the application

Check the running container:

sudo docker ps

Check the application health:

curl http://localhost:5000/health

Expected output:

{"status":"healthy"}

Test the home page:

curl http://localhost:5000/

Step 10: Open the application in your browser

Open:

http://localhost:5000

You should see:

    Hello from Python Flask! Running inside Docker on Ubuntu 🚀

Health endpoint:

http://localhost:5000/health
Step 11: Useful Docker commands

View application logs:

sudo docker logs -f flask-container

Stop the container:

sudo docker stop flask-container

Start the container again:

sudo docker start flask-container

Restart the container:
